  "pinned": false,
  "description": "# Conversation Summary\n\n1. **Initial Request**: User provided a Vue.js team collaboration application with multiple components for managing teams, channels, categories, and members, along with a Vuex store structure.\n\n2. **User Action**: Requested modification to the `AddMemberDialog.vue` component to use a user list selector instead of a text input for adding members to teams.\n\n3. **Solution Implemented**: Refactored the component to include a dropdown selector that dynamically loads available users from the `$storex.users.allUsers` store, filtering out users already in the team.\n\n4. **Key Improvements**: Added `onUserSelected()` method for handling user selection, implemented `availableUsers` computed property to prevent duplicates, and updated the preview member logic to use selected user data.\n\n5. **Component Standards**: Maintained consistent Vue component structure with script setup, template, and export default object following the project's VueDeveloper profile requirements.",
